{"name":"Raftsman","hex":"#3c5f9b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"raftsman","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person who transports a raft of floating logs downstream to a sawmill; a rafter."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raftsman"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raft","blocks":[{"text":"A raft is any flat structure for support or transportation over water. It is usually of basic design, characterized by the absence of a hull. Rafts are usually kept afloat by using any combination of buoyant materials such as wood, sealed barrels, or inflated air chambers and are typically not propelled by an engine. Rafts are an ancient mode of transport; naturally occurring rafts such as entwined vegetation and pieces of wood have been used to traverse water since the dawn of humanity."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Huck_and_jim_on_raft.jpg/330px-Huck_and_jim_on_raft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raft","wikidata":"Q200433"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Huck_and_jim_on_raft.jpg/500px-Huck_and_jim_on_raft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a0/Huck_and_jim_on_raft.jpg/500px-Huck_and_jim_on_raft.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Traditional raft, from the 1884 edition of Adventures of Huckleberry Finn","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHuck-and-jim-on-raft.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Raft_guara.jpg/500px-Raft_guara.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ef/Raft_guara.jpg/1280px-Raft_guara.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"ht